──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FULL-APP BUILD: ERROR ATTRIBUTION (why DEFERRED, with evidence)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ACTIVEORDERS_ERRORS = 0  (iOS) and 0 (macOS).  Zero errors originate in this surface.
  Root cause is PRE-EXISTING, UNRELATED parallel-merge baseline breakage — the same precedent
  recorded in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md (P-0010 ToolCard) and P-0006 InfrastructureSection:
    • `public struct DashboardWidgetSize` redeclared in 15 files across
      Sources/DashboardWidgets/* + TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/*  → "ambiguous for type lookup".
    • `public enum PowerFlowConnection` redeclared in 2 files (same cause).
    • Downstream: VehicleHero{Model,Projection,Connection,Update,…}, TelemetryErrorsModel
      ambiguous → ~720 "cannot infer key path type" cascades. ALL in *Widget*/dashboard-widgets
      (iOS) and the same + collateral sibling panels (macOS).
    • Co-located *.Tests.swift import XCTest into the app target → needs ENABLE_TESTING_SEARCH_PATHS
      (applied; resolved).
    • macOS app bundle needs a development signing identity (CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO used for build).
  These are outside this prompt's allowed files (ActiveOrdersSection.*). The shared Sources/ group
  feeds BOTH app targets (ADR-002), so the same collisions block iOS and macOS identically. Per the
  established P4-apple disposition, the full-app `build test` is DEFERRED to the
  p4-apple/P99-0001-apple-acceptance-gate (macos-latest, signing identities, after the widget-slot
  de-duplication merge); this surface is independently verified green above.

